iOS 27.3 adds a new "Selfie Sing" feature in <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-music/">Apple Music</a> that lets users record themselves while singing a song.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/ios-27-3-selfie-sing.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1075522" /><br/>
There's a dedicated Selfie Sing playlist and a selfie camera view that shows lyrics on the screen while also recording a video. Apple has a description of the feature:<br/>
<blockquote>There are some songs everyone knows by heart, the ones that come on and suddenly the whole room's singing along. This playlist is loaded with them, each one ready to become your next Selfie Sing. Pick your favorite, record a Selfie Sing, add mic effects to your voice, then save or share your video selfie with anyone you like. No pitch-perfect anything required–just you, the song, and the moment. Oh, and make sure you've updated to the latest iOS before getting started.</blockquote><br/>
After selecting a song, you can tap on the camera icon to start a Selfie Sing. Tapping the red button begins a recording, and the lyrics start to scroll by. When a song is finished, there are options to change the volume of your voice or add an effect. Options include Megaphone, Echo, Concert Hall, and Studio. Videos can then be saved to the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/photos/">Photos</a> library or shared.<br/>
